event sink
  1. receives only the kinds it subscribes to
     expected: events of the kinds the factory declares arrive, events of the other kinds do not
  2. receives events in batches
     expected: 25 events published with batchSize 10 arrive complete, in batches of at most 10, in fewer than 25 batches
  3. drops and counts events instead of blocking the publisher when the buffer is full
     expected: with a stalled external system and a buffer of 5, publishing 200 events returns within 200ms and counts all but a handful as dropped (buffer_full)
  4. delivers the buffered events on shutdown
     expected: 10 buffered events, none flushed yet by size or age, are delivered on Close, and none is counted as dropped
  5. returns from shutdown within its context while the external system stalls
     expected: Close returns within its context of 200ms while the external system stalls, and counts the 10 undelivered events as dropped (shutdown)
  6. delivers a batch the external system refused for now once it accepts again
     expected: 5 events refused for now are delivered after the external system accepts again, and none is dropped
  7. does not repeat a batch the external system refused for good
     expected: 5 events refused for good are counted as dropped (permanent) and never delivered, even after the external system accepts again
  8. rejects an invalid configuration naming the faulty value
     expected: the factory rejects the configuration with an error that contains "bogus"
